bound-lock/1 about="a cell is in one of four states: FREE, REQUIRED, FORBIDDEN, CONFLICT — green, grey, red, fork are their renders" at=policy:law/D3 by=target form=alphabet kind=definition measure=status needs=samples/yes/D3-state.json|vectors/states.json|vectors/states-per-step.json|vectors/units-16.json|vectors/transitions.json restsOn=law/D2-ideal role=demands scope=law/D3-state value=present view=ideal
bound-lock/1 about="the debit of a cell is log2 of the states between its floor and ceiling; a closed cell has zero" at=policy:law/D4 by=target form=alphabet kind=definition measure=status needs=samples/yes/D4-debit-in-bits.json|vectors/freedom.json|vectors/debits.json restsOn=law/A0-carrier|law/A3-resolution role=demands scope=law/D4-debit-in-bits value=present view=chain
bound-lock/1 about="a declaration is a demand u and a limit w on a valued lattice; its cost is forced by two axioms" at=policy:law/D5 by=target form=alphabet kind=definition measure=status needs=vectors/declaration.json restsOn=law/A0-carrier role=demands scope=law/D5-declaration value=present view=valuation
bound-lock/1 about="the premium of a cell is what closing it costs: the residual information under the declaration" at=policy:law/D6 by=target form=alphabet kind=definition measure=status needs=vectors/premium.json restsOn=law/D5-declaration|law/D4-debit-in-bits role=demands scope=law/D6-premium value=present view=valuation
bound-lock/1 about="two incomparable bounds on one cell from two signers; rendered with both, closed only by a signature" at=policy:law/D7 by=target form=alphabet kind=definition measure=status needs=vectors/atom/ledger.json restsOn=law/A2-meet role=demands scope=law/D7-fork value=present view=lattice
bound-lock/1 about="the present is the meet of overlapping observation bands; there is no instant to certify" at=policy:law/D8 by=target form=alphabet kind=definition measure=status needs=samples/yes/D8-present.json|vectors/info/present-meet.json restsOn=law/A4-epoch|law/A3-resolution role=demands scope=law/D8-present value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="an origin's yield is bits it closed minus bits reopened against it, per act, over an epoch" at=policy:law/D9 by=target form=alphabet kind=definition measure=status needs=samples/yes/D9-yield.json restsOn=law/A5-origin-is-extension|law/D4-debit-in-bits role=demands scope=law/D9-yield value=present view=valuation
bound-lock/1 about="a signed ceiling with no origin: a question with form, resolution, premium, dependents and a cheapest closer" at=policy:law/D10 by=target form=alphabet kind=definition measure=status needs=samples/yes/D10-open-question.json restsOn=law/A0-carrier|law/A1-encounter|law/D6-premium role=demands scope=law/D10-open-question value=present view=valuation
bound-lock/1 about="The graph identity — If $x\\wedge y=\\bot$ then \\[ \\RI_H(x,y)\\;=\\;\\log_2 n-\\frac{\\Phi(x,y)}{n}, \\qquad \\Phi(x,y)=\\sum_{e}c_e\\log_2\\frac{a_e\\,b_e}{c_e}, \\] the sum running over the edges of $G(x,y)$, where $c_e$ is the weight of $e$ and $a_e,b_e$ are the sizes of the two blocks it joins." at=policy:law/lem-identity by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/lem-identity.json restsOn=law/A0-carrier|law/A2-meet|law/D5-declaration role=demands scope=law/lem-identity value=present view=spectrum
bound-lock/1 about="Every coarsening step costs two — For integers $p,q\\ge1$, $\\varphi(p+q)-\\varphi(p)-\\varphi(q)\\ge2$, with equality exactly at $p=q=1$. Consequently, if $P$ coarsens $Q$ from $|Q|$ blocks to $|P|$ blocks then $\\Sigma(P)-\\Sigma(Q)\\ge2\\bigl(|Q|-|P|\\bigr)$." at=policy:law/lem-merge by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/lem-merge.json restsOn=law/A0-carrier|law/A2-meet|law/D5-declaration role=demands scope=law/lem-merge value=present view=spectrum
bound-lock/1 about="Reduction to a discrete join — Every pair with trivial meet can be transformed, without decreasing $\\RI_H$ and in finitely many steps, into a pair on the same $n$ states with trivial meet and discrete join." at=policy:law/lem-join by=target form=alphabet kind=corollary measure=status needs=samples/yes/lem-join.json restsOn=law/lem-identity role=demands scope=law/lem-join value=present view=spectrum
bound-lock/1 about="Reduction to a trivial meet — Let $\\tau(N)$ denote the maximum of $\\RI_H$ over pairs on $N$ states with trivial meet. Then for any $x,y\\in\\Pin$ with $x\\wedge y$ having blocks of sizes $n_1,\\dots,n_r$, \\[ \\RI_H(x,y)=\\sum_{t=1}^{r}\\frac{n_t}{n}\\,\\RI_H\\bigl(x|_{B_t},y|_{B_t}\\bigr) \\;\\le\\;\\sum_t \\frac{n_t}{n}\\,\\tau(n_t). \\] Each restricted pair has trivial meet. If $\\tau$ is non-decreasing the bound is $\\tau(n)$; and if $\\tau$ is moreover strictly increasing above $N=2$, equality for $n\\ge3$ forces $r=1$." at=policy:law/lem-meet by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/lem-meet.json restsOn=law/lem-identity|law/prop-cmi role=demands scope=law/lem-meet value=present view=spectrum
bound-lock/1 about="Components, and the mediant — Both $\\Sigma(m)-\\Sigma(u)$ and $\\Sigma(w)-\\Sigma(j)$ decompose as sums over the blocks of $m$, which are the connected components of the block graph $G(u,w)$; and a component contributing $0$ to the denominator contributes $0$ to the numerator. Hence the ratio is at most the largest ratio of a single component, each of which is a declaration on $n_t\\le n$ states with trivial meet." at=policy:law/lem-mediant by=target form=alphabet kind=corollary measure=status needs=vectors/blocks.json restsOn=law/lem-merge role=demands scope=law/lem-mediant value=present view=spectrum
bound-lock/1 about="The integer inequality — For every integer $t\\ge1$, $\\varphi(t)\\ge 2(t-1)$, with equality exactly at $t\\in\\{1,2\\}$." at=policy:law/lem-phi by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/lem-phi.json restsOn=law/lem-join|law/lem-meet role=demands scope=law/lem-phi value=present view=spectrum
bound-lock/1 about="The extremal — For every $n\\ge1$, \\[ c_n\\;=\\;\\log_2 n-2+\\frac{2}{n}, \\] and for $n\\ge3$ the maximum is attained exactly at the following configuration and its relabellings (for $n\\le2$ the maximum is $0$ and every pair attains it): identify the $n$ states with the $n$ edges of a path on $n+1$ vertices; let $x$ group the edges sharing an even-numbered endpoint and $y$ those sharing an odd-numbered endpoint. These have $\\lceil (n+1)/2\\rceil$ and $\\lfloor (n+1)/2\\rfloor$ blocks, every block of size $1$ or $2$, trivial meet and discrete join." at=policy:law/thm-extremal by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/thm-extremal.json restsOn=law/lem-identity|law/lem-join|law/lem-meet|law/lem-phi role=demands scope=law/thm-extremal value=present view=spectrum
bound-lock/1 about="The retreat ratio — For every $n\\ge2$, over declarations in conflict on $\\Pin$ under Shannon entropy, \\[ \\max\\frac{\\viol_H}{\\viols_H}\\;=\\;\\rho(n)\\;:=\\;\\frac{n}{2}\\,H_{bal}(n,2) \\;=\\;\\frac{\\varphi(n)-\\varphi\\bigl(\\lceil\\tfrac n2\\rceil\\bigr) -\\varphi\\bigl(\\lfloor\\tfrac n2\\rfloor\\bigr)}{2}, \\] attained exactly when the demand $u$ is a balanced two-block partition, the block graph is connected, and the limit merges two singletons of $u\\vee w$. In particular the maximum equals $n/2$ exactly for even $n$, and $n/2-\\Theta(1/n)$ for odd $n$." at=policy:law/thm-ratio by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/thm-ratio.json restsOn=law/lem-mediant|law/lem-merge role=demands scope=law/thm-ratio value=present view=spectrum
bound-lock/1 about="The gap, exactly — For every lattice and every monotone $f$, \\[ g(u,w)\\;=\\;\\max\\bigl\\{\\,f(p)+f(q)-f(p\\vee q)\\;:\\;p\\le u,\\ q\\le w\\,\\bigr\\}\\;-\\;f(m), \\] the maximum being at least $f(m)$, as $p=q=m$ shows." at=policy:law/thm-gap by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=vectors/premium.json|vectors/hypothesis.json restsOn=law/A0-carrier|law/A2-meet|law/D5-declaration role=demands scope=law/thm-gap value=present view=valuation
bound-lock/1 about="Collapse, and its converse — The following are equivalent for a monotone valuation $f$. · $f$ has the data-processing property. · For every $u,w$: $\\viols_f(u,w)=f(u\\vee w)-f(w)$, attained at $S=u\\vee w$. · For every $u,w$: $g(u,w)=\\RI_f(u,w)$." at=policy:law/thm-collapse by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=vectors/premium.json|vectors/supermodular.json restsOn=law/D6-premium|law/thm-gap role=demands scope=law/thm-collapse value=present view=valuation
bound-lock/1 about="Degeneration — $g\\equiv0$ --- retreat is optimal for every declaration --- if and only if $f$ is supermodular, $f(x)+f(y)\\le f(x\\vee y)+f(x\\wedge y)$ for all $x,y$. Modular valuations are the special case of equality." at=policy:law/thm-modular by=target form=alphabet kind=corollary measure=status needs=vectors/supermodular.json restsOn=law/thm-gap role=demands scope=law/thm-modular value=present view=valuation
bound-lock/1 about="Retreat is locally optimal — For every lattice and every monotone $f$, the retreat $S_0=m$ is a weak local minimum of $C$ with respect to cover moves." at=policy:law/thm-local by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/thm-local.json restsOn=law/A0-carrier|law/A2-meet|law/D5-declaration role=demands scope=law/thm-local value=present view=valuation
bound-lock/1 about="cf. — $\\RI_H(x,y)=I(x;y\\mid x\\wedge y)$." at=policy:law/prop-cmi by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/prop-cmi.json restsOn=law/A0-carrier|law/A2-meet|law/D5-declaration role=demands scope=law/prop-cmi value=present view=valuation
bound-lock/1 about="Both costs, decomposed — For every declaration on $L$, with $u,w,m,j$ as usual and $\\viol_i,g_i$ computed from $f_i$ on coordinate $i$, \\[ \\viol_f \\;=\\; \\viol_1+\\viol_2+\\bigl[D(u)-D(m)\\bigr], \\qquad g_f \\;=\\; g_1+g_2+\\RI_D(u,w), \\] the second under the data-processing property for $f,f_1,f_2$." at=policy:law/prop-dep by=target form=alphabet kind=corollary measure=status needs=samples/yes/prop-dep.json restsOn=law/thm-collapse role=demands scope=law/prop-dep value=present view=valuation
bound-lock/1 about="Mutual information is a planning premium — Take the declaration that demands the first subsystem be answerable and forbids the state to exceed the second: $u=(\\top,\\bot)$, $w=(\\bot,\\top)$. Then \\[ \\viol_f=H(X),\\qquad \\viols_f=H(X\\mid Y),\\qquad g_f=I_\\mu(X;Y), \\] while $g_1=g_2=0$." at=policy:law/thm-mi by=target form=alphabet kind=corollary measure=status needs=samples/yes/thm-mi.json restsOn=law/thm-collapse role=demands scope=law/thm-mi value=present view=valuation
bound-lock/1 about="Additivity up to the mutual information — For every declaration on a product of two subsystems under a joint measure, \\[ \\viol_1+\\viol_2-I_\\mu\\;\\le\\;\\viol_f\\;\\le\\;\\viol_1+\\viol_2, \\qquad \\bigl|\\,g_f-(g_1+g_2)\\,\\bigr|\\;\\le\\;I_\\mu . \\] The conflict is therefore always discounted by dependence and never inflated, while the premium is always inflated and never discounted by more than the same amount. Both ends that are reached are reached by different declarations: the left inequality on the conflict at $u=\\top$, $w=\\bot$, and $g_f=g_1+g_2+I_\\mu$ at the crossed declaration of Theorem . The lower end of the band on the premium is not known to be attained, and Remark says what reaching it would require." at=policy:law/thm-dep by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/thm-dep.json restsOn=law/prop-dep|law/thm-mi role=demands scope=law/thm-dep value=present view=valuation
bound-lock/1 about="c_n = log2 n − 2 + 2/n bounds a pairwise audit's conservativeness in bits" at=policy:law/T13 by=target form=alphabet kind=corollary measure=status needs=samples/yes/T13-c_n.json restsOn=law/D6-premium role=demands scope=law/T13-c_n value=present view=valuation
bound-lock/1 about="premium is zero iff the valuation is supermodular there: a second origin adds nothing" at=policy:law/T14 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=vectors/field-uses.json|vectors/hypothesis.json restsOn=law/D6-premium|law/A1-encounter role=demands scope=law/T14-supermodular-degeneration value=present view=valuation
bound-lock/1 about="the premium equals residual information exactly for valuations with the data-processing property" at=policy:law/T15 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=vectors/premium.json|vectors/slack.json restsOn=law/D6-premium|law/thm-gap role=demands scope=law/T15-premium-is-residual-information value=present view=valuation
bound-lock/1 about="Exact decomposition — On every finite lattice $u=\\bigvee\\{j\\in\\JI(L):j\\le u\\}$ and $w=\\bigwedge\\{m\\in\\MI(L):w\\le m\\}$. Hence $\\reg$ is injective: a declaration is its register, with nothing lost." at=policy:law/thm-decomp by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=vectors/register.json|vectors/incidence.json restsOn=law/D2-ideal|law/D3-state role=demands scope=law/thm-decomp value=present view=ideal
bound-lock/1 about="Half Boolean — For every finite lattice and every debit $j$, the limit side is truth-functional: $j\\le w_1\\wedge w_2$ iff $j\\le w_1$ and $j\\le w_2$. The demand side --- whether $j\\le u_1\\vee u_2$ is determined by $(j\\le u_1,\\ j\\le u_2)$ --- is truth-functional if and only if $L$ is distributive." at=policy:law/prop-halfboolean by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=vectors/boolean.json|vectors/bit-loss.json restsOn=law/D2-ideal|law/D3-state role=demands scope=law/prop-halfboolean value=present view=complement
bound-lock/1 about="What is additive under independence, and what is not — Let $L=L_1\\times L_2$ with each factor of at least two elements, and let $f=f_1\\oplus f_2$. Then $\\viol_f$ and $\\viols_f$ are exactly additive on product declarations: two-sided constraints admit no economy of scale under independence. The vocabulary is not: \\[ \\delta(L_1\\times L_2)\\;=\\;|L_1||L_2|-|MI(L_1)|-|MI(L_2)|, \\] which exceeds $\\delta(L_1)+\\delta(L_2)$ by exactly $(|L_1|-1)(|L_2|-1)-1$, strictly unless both factors are the two-element lattice." at=policy:law/prop-additive by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/prop-additive.json restsOn=law/D2-ideal|law/D3-state role=demands scope=law/prop-additive value=present view=valuation
bound-lock/1 about="The witness — Let $F$ be in conflict. Then $F$ is sound for every monotone valuation if and only if \\[ \\textrm{(W)}\\qquad u\\in A\\quadand\\quad \\exists\\,b\\in B:\\ u\\wedge b=m . \\]" at=policy:law/thm-witness by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/thm-witness.json restsOn=law/D2-ideal|law/D3-state role=demands scope=law/thm-witness value=present view=valuation
bound-lock/1 about="a withdrawal is exact iff the scale is distributive" at=policy:law/T8 by=target form=alphabet kind=corollary measure=status needs=vectors/coherence.json restsOn=law/D2-ideal role=demands scope=law/T8-exact-withdrawal value=present view=complement
bound-lock/1 about="an origin that moves a verdict carries at least the bits by which it reduces the cell's debit, and exactly those suffice" at=policy:law/T1 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T1-only-verdict-bits-travel.json|samples/no/T1-only-verdict-bits-travel.json restsOn=law/D4-debit-in-bits|law/A2-meet role=demands scope=law/T1-only-verdict-bits-travel value=present view=chain
bound-lock/1 about="a new coordinate appears exactly where two origins disagree at the same resolution" at=policy:law/T2 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T2-coordinate-where-disagree.json restsOn=law/A1-encounter|law/D0-coordinate role=demands scope=law/T2-coordinate-where-disagree value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="two heads folding the same claims converge to one fold; the fixed point is unique" at=policy:law/T3 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=vectors/region.json|vectors/atom/formula.json restsOn=law/A2-meet|law/A1-encounter role=demands scope=law/T3-fixed-point value=present view=product
bound-lock/1 about="receipts compose in any order; the fold of a union is the meet of the folds" at=policy:law/T4 by=target form=alphabet kind=remark measure=status needs=vectors/effective.json|vectors/reach.json|vectors/atom/locks-are-targets.json restsOn=law/A2-meet role=demands scope=law/T4-composition value=present view=product
bound-lock/1 about="a claim coarsened to a lower resolution fits at least as many regions" at=policy:law/T5 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T5-coarsen-widens.json|samples/no/T5-coarsen-widens.json|vectors/info/coarsen-fit.json restsOn=law/A3-resolution|law/A6-vacuity role=demands scope=law/T5-coarsen-widens value=present view=chain
bound-lock/1 about="the width of the present is maturation rate minus forgetting rate; a system with only past or only future has no present" at=policy:law/T6 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T6-present-converges.json|samples/no/T6-present-converges.json|vectors/info/present-convergence.json restsOn=law/D8-present|law/A6-vacuity role=demands scope=law/T6-present-converges value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="for every verdict there is a coarsest resolution that still moves it, strictly coarser than the finest available" at=policy:law/T7 by=target form=alphabet kind=corollary measure=status needs=samples/yes/T7-sufficient-resolution.json|samples/no/A3-resolution.json|vectors/info/sufficient-resolution.json restsOn=law/A3-resolution role=demands scope=law/T7-sufficient-resolution value=present view=chain
bound-lock/1 about="a system folded by its own ceilings converges to what its encounters recognize; the residue is unique" at=policy:law/T9 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T9-self-application.json|vectors/atom/verdict.json|vectors/laws-as-folds.json restsOn=law/A6-vacuity|law/A1-encounter|law/A9-everything-is-a-bound role=demands scope=law/T9-self-application-converges value=present view=quotient
bound-lock/1 about="two definitions of one question diverge without either failing; the divergence is invisible until an encounter joins them" at=policy:law/T10 by=target form=alphabet kind=corollary measure=status needs=samples/yes/T10-drift.json|samples/no/T10-drift.json|vectors/drift.json restsOn=law/A5-origin-is-extension role=demands scope=law/T10-drift value=present view=quotient
bound-lock/1 about="the size of a body of knowledge is its count of distinct questions with an encounter; the rest is drift" at=policy:law/T11 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T11-size-is-questions.json|samples/no/T11-size-is-questions.json|vectors/questions.json restsOn=law/T10-drift|law/A6-vacuity role=demands scope=law/T11-size-is-questions value=present view=quotient
bound-lock/1 about="the fraction of a domain's claims that are facts equals its second-origin rate; drift and surviving falsehood are its complement" at=policy:law/T12 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T12-reliability-is-encounter-rate.json|samples/no/T12-reliability-is-encounter-rate.json restsOn=law/A1-encounter|law/T10-drift role=demands scope=law/T12-reliability-is-encounter-rate value=present view=valuation
bound-lock/1 about="an independent second origin never raises a cell's debit: it falls by log2 of the states it leaves standing, a full bit exactly when it admits at most half of them, and nothing exactly when it narrows nothing" at=policy:law/T16 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T16-encounter-inequality.json|samples/no/T16-encounter-inequality.json restsOn=law/A1-encounter|law/D4-debit-in-bits|law/T14-supermodular-degeneration role=demands scope=law/T16-encounter-inequality value=present view=chain
bound-lock/1 about="no claim shorter than the debit reduction moves a verdict; none longer is needed" at=policy:law/T17 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=vectors/complexity.json restsOn=law/T1-only-verdict-bits-travel|law/D4-debit-in-bits role=demands scope=law/T17-coding-of-verdicts value=present view=chain
bound-lock/1 about="closed bits with a second origin are scarce, unforgeable, measurable, transferable and third-party verifiable; no issuer exists" at=policy:law/T18 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T18-freedom-is-a-currency.json restsOn=law/A7-freedom-conserved|law/D9-yield|law/A5-origin-is-extension role=demands scope=law/T18-freedom-is-a-currency value=present view=valuation
bound-lock/1 about="two signed bounds on one cell fold by form: narrower wins, equal is an encounter, incomparable is a fork; nothing is ever replaced" at=policy:law/T19 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T19-signatures-fold.json|vectors/signatures.json restsOn=law/A2-meet|law/D7-fork role=demands scope=law/T19-signatures-fold value=present view=lattice
bound-lock/1 about="a region's age is the encounters since its last observation, not elapsed clock; the width of its present is the inverse of its encounter rate" at=policy:law/T20 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T20-age-is-encounters.json|samples/no/T20-age-is-encounters.json restsOn=law/A4-epoch|law/A1-encounter|law/D8-present role=demands scope=law/T20-age-is-encounters value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="a reading is a claim by the reader on the cell at its resolution — a weak encounter; undisputed density is agreement" at=policy:law/T21 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T21-reading-is-an-origin.json|vectors/atom/derived.json restsOn=law/A5-origin-is-extension|law/A1-encounter role=demands scope=law/T21-reading-is-an-origin value=present view=galois
bound-lock/1 about="two claims fold when their epochs meet and their intervals meet; epochs that meet with intervals that do not are a fork, and epochs that do not meet are no encounter at all" at=policy:law/T22 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T22-fold-is-superposition.json restsOn=law/A2-meet|law/A4-epoch|law/A1-encounter role=demands scope=law/T22-fold-is-superposition value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="two origins meet at the common multiple of their periods, so a domain has a spectrum of resolutions where encounters happen; read coarser, a claim recovers the fine cells that lay under it" at=policy:law/T23 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T23-domain-has-a-spectrum.json restsOn=law/T22-fold-is-superposition|law/T20-age-is-encounters|law/A3-resolution role=demands scope=law/T23-domain-has-a-spectrum value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="what is not known has coordinates: the open questions rank by premium against dependents and cost, and a small head of that order holds most of the value" at=policy:law/T24 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T24-ignorance-has-coordinates.json restsOn=law/D10-open-question|law/A7-freedom-conserved role=demands scope=law/T24-ignorance-has-coordinates value=present view=valuation
bound-lock/1 about="counted by mentions, a corpus of rules grows vacuous without bound; counted by the verdicts they move, vacuity converges: a rule earns its place by moving a verdict" at=policy:law/T25 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T25-rules-earn-their-place.json restsOn=law/A6-vacuity|law/T1-only-verdict-bits-travel|law/T2-coordinate-where-disagree role=demands scope=law/T25-rules-earn-their-place value=present view=quotient
bound-lock/1 about="knowing grows by disagreement: most cells are born where two origins split, and what stays grey is a small remainder" at=policy:law/T26 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T26-knowing-has-four-states.json restsOn=law/A9-everything-is-a-bound|law/A8-four-states|law/A1-encounter role=demands scope=law/T26-knowing-has-four-states value=present view=lattice
bound-lock/1 about="spending a budget where the premium is highest closes more than spending it blindly, and provoking the disagreement closes more still and names coordinates that were not there" at=policy:law/T27 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T27-disagreement-can-be-provoked.json restsOn=law/T2-coordinate-where-disagree|law/A7-freedom-conserved|law/A5-origin-is-extension role=demands scope=law/T27-disagreement-can-be-provoked value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="resolution times independent encounters per cell stays above a floor c; the sufficient resolution is where the product saturates" at=policy:law/H1-uncertainty by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/H1-uncertainty.json|samples/no/H1-uncertainty.json restsOn=law/A3-resolution|law/A1-encounter role=demands scope=law/H1-uncertainty value=present view=chain
bound-lock/1 about="n origins on a cell agree at a resolution; raising it opens agreements into forks, each a coordinate the coarser scale hid; the sufficient resolution of a region is where its residual figure stops changing" at=policy:law/T36 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T36-agreement-has-a-resolution.json restsOn=law/A3-resolution|law/T2-coordinate-where-disagree|law/T7-sufficient-resolution role=demands scope=law/T36-agreement-has-a-resolution value=present view=chain
bound-lock/1 about="stretching every ceiling by one factor separates what no width can hold, a cell whose origins do not meet, from a ceiling that was merely tight; pouring another world into a lock counts the places it fills; and a lock deforms with use, what was touched closing toward what was seen there and what was not opening, toward the shape the world gives it" at=policy:law/T37 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T37-a-lock-is-a-mould.json restsOn=law/A0-carrier|law/A6-vacuity|law/T25-rules-earn-their-place|law/T36-agreement-has-a-resolution role=demands scope=law/T37-a-lock-is-a-mould value=present view=dual
bound-lock/1 about="n independent origins on a cell are the vertices of a polygon whose interior is their meet: two an edge, three an area, four a vertex the others do not enclose, five a verdict that holds without any one of them, and beyond that a meet that narrows toward consensus — a meet that never closes at any n is two cells wearing one name" at=policy:law/T38 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T38-origins-are-a-polygon.json restsOn=law/A1-encounter|law/A2-meet|law/A5-origin-is-extension|law/T2-coordinate-where-disagree role=demands scope=law/T38-origins-are-a-polygon value=present view=product
bound-lock/1 about="the independence of two origins is the distance between their extensions: one extension is one origin, disjoint extensions share nothing" at=policy:law/C1 by=target form=alphabet kind=corollary measure=status needs=samples/yes/C1-independence-is-distance.json restsOn=law/A5-origin-is-extension role=demands scope=law/C1-independence-is-distance value=present view=galois
bound-lock/1 about="one claim per generation is admitted without a second origin; a second such claim is a fork" at=policy:law/C3 by=target form=alphabet kind=corollary measure=status needs=samples/yes/C3-bootstrap-once.json restsOn=law/A1-encounter|law/A4-epoch role=demands scope=law/C3-bootstrap-once value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="Data processing forces submodularity — Every valuation with the data-processing property is submodular. Among such valuations, $g\\equiv0$ if and only if $f$ is modular." at=policy:law/C4 by=target form=alphabet kind=corollary measure=status needs=vectors/hypothesis.json restsOn=law/thm-collapse|law/thm-modular role=demands scope=law/C4-dpi-subadditive value=present view=valuation
bound-lock/1 about="where reading already is, the next reading lands: over eight epochs of placement in proportion to the origins a cell already carries, the ratio between the densest tenth and the sparsest rises at every epoch and the deserts stay empty, while the same budget placed blind to density holds that ratio near two and touches three times as many cells" at=policy:law/H2 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/H2-density-attracts.json|samples/no/H2-density-attracts.json restsOn=law/A1-encounter|law/A6-vacuity role=demands scope=law/H2-density-attracts value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="a cell grows until something stops it: a wall the lock names, or the place where the next origin is nearer than its own, so a cell alone between two walls is as wide as they leave it and one that lands beside another takes the midpoint; what stops a cell is never its own doing, and an origin landing beside it narrows it and widens nothing" at=policy:law/T39 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T39-cells-grow-until-stopped.json restsOn=law/A0-carrier|law/A1-encounter|law/A3-resolution|law/T7-sufficient-resolution role=demands scope=law/T39-cells-grow-until-stopped value=present view=product
bound-lock/1 about="what knowing costs is not set by how many origins look but by where they land: one budget of two hundred gives a ratio near two placed blind and above twenty placed where reading already is, so the shape of what is known is a fact about placement, and it leaves cities and deserts in one field" at=policy:law/T40 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T40-cost-by-density.json restsOn=law/T38-origins-are-a-polygon|law/T27-disagreement-can-be-provoked|law/T18-freedom-is-a-currency role=demands scope=law/T40-cost-by-density value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="two cells are one step apart when an origin looked at both, so a world is the graph of its lookings and distance is the walk between them: zero on a cell against itself, symmetric, never shortened by a third cell, and across a desert no looking crosses there is no number at all, which is the horizon" at=policy:law/T41 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T41-distance-is-the-walk-between-lookings.json restsOn=law/T40-cost-by-density|law/T23-domain-has-a-spectrum|law/T2-coordinate-where-disagree role=demands scope=law/T41-distance-is-the-walk-between-lookings value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="two observers of one world hold their own origins and read the same cells differently, and that is not a contradiction: wherever they hold the same origins at a cell they agree, every time, so the disagreement is the difference of their horizons and never of the world" at=policy:law/T42 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T42-no-privileged-observer.json restsOn=law/A5-origin-is-extension|law/A9-everything-is-a-bound|law/A4-epoch|law/D8-present|law/T40-cost-by-density|law/T17-coding-of-verdicts role=demands scope=law/T42-no-privileged-observer value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="information and distance are two readings of one thing: with no origin there is neither a fact nor a finite distance, and each origin that lands gives exactly one of each" at=policy:law/T43 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T43-each-origin-gives-one-fact-and-one-distance.json restsOn=law/A1-encounter|law/A9-everything-is-a-bound|law/T41-distance-is-the-walk-between-lookings|law/A6-vacuity role=demands scope=law/T43-each-origin-gives-one-fact-and-one-distance value=present view=galois
bound-lock/1 about="one claim of one width is worth what it connects: nothing inside a city where every pair already had a walk, one pair between two lone cells, and the product of two components when it lands across a desert, so where to look is a question with an answer and the answer is read before the claim lands" at=policy:law/T44 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T44-an-origin-is-worth-its-reach.json restsOn=law/T41-distance-is-the-walk-between-lookings|law/T27-disagreement-can-be-provoked|law/T18-freedom-is-a-currency|law/A5-origin-is-extension role=demands scope=law/T44-an-origin-is-worth-its-reach value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="cells that rest on one bound move together when it moves: narrowing a ceiling turns cells red with nobody looking at them, some past the horizon of whoever signed it, and the effect is the bound's and not the order's, since the same narrowing taken in two steps names exactly the cells it names in one" at=policy:law/T45 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T45-cells-that-rest-on-one-bound-are-entangled.json restsOn=law/A0-carrier|law/A9-everything-is-a-bound|law/T19-signatures-fold|law/T41-distance-is-the-walk-between-lookings role=demands scope=law/T45-cells-that-rest-on-one-bound-are-entangled value=present view=product
bound-lock/1 about="a world changes in two ways at once: looking travels and stops at the horizon, a bound does not travel and carries no step, so moving it changes cells no walk reaches; counting the bound as if it were a looking would make the whole world one neighbourhood, which is how the two are told apart" at=policy:law/T46 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T46-a-bound-moves-cells-no-walk-reaches.json restsOn=law/A0-carrier|law/T41-distance-is-the-walk-between-lookings|law/T45-cells-that-rest-on-one-bound-are-entangled role=demands scope=law/T46-a-bound-moves-cells-no-walk-reaches value=present view=lattice
bound-lock/1 about="one coordinate on a scale of a hundred and five levels is superposed at six point seven bits, definite when two claims meet at one level, and forbidden rather than narrow when a ceiling falls under that floor, while a second coordinate resting on the bound that moved narrows to five point four bits with nobody measuring it" at=policy:law/T47 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T47-a-two-pole-object.json restsOn=law/A0-carrier|law/A7-freedom-conserved|law/D4-debit-in-bits|law/T45-cells-that-rest-on-one-bound-are-entangled|law/T46-a-bound-moves-cells-no-walk-reaches role=demands scope=law/T47-a-two-pole-object value=present view=lattice
bound-lock/1 about="an epoch is a phase: claims arriving at one turn of a period reinforce and claims half a period apart cancel, so sweeping the delay of half of them draws the period's own shape, and observing one route, which is fixing when those claims arrived, moves the pattern to its complement" at=policy:law/T48 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T48-epoch-is-phase.json restsOn=law/A4-epoch|law/T22-fold-is-superposition|law/T45-cells-that-rest-on-one-bound-are-entangled role=demands scope=law/T48-epoch-is-phase value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="a claim carries a size and a direction, how much it narrows and the turn it landed on, and a withdrawal is the same size the other way: two hundred claims in phase make the square of their number and the same two hundred strewn make its order, while a write and its withdrawal at one epoch leave nothing and at different epochs do not cancel" at=policy:law/T49 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T49-amplitude-has-sign-and-phase.json restsOn=law/T48-epoch-is-phase|law/T19-signatures-fold|law/A4-epoch|law/A1-encounter role=demands scope=law/T49-amplitude-has-sign-and-phase value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="stated as a hint and never as a claim about the world: if what is is a field of floors and ceilings, a distant signature changes a cell whose own record never moved, and in two hundred trials of one cell holding one value the verdict came out both ways, so nothing stored at the cell explains the difference and what explains it is the bound the cell rests on; the resemblance is structural and never arithmetic, with no continuous amplitudes and no inequality violated by number; structural resemblance, one origin, not a claim about the world" at=policy:law/H3 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/H3-a-distant-signature-moves-a-cell-that-did-not-move.json|samples/no/H3-a-distant-signature-moves-a-cell-that-did-not-move.json restsOn=law/T46-a-bound-moves-cells-no-walk-reaches|law/T47-a-two-pole-object role=demands scope=law/H3-a-distant-signature-moves-a-cell-that-did-not-move value=present view=lattice
bound-lock/1 about="the object is c = ⟨⊥, ⊤, O, ⊑⟩ over L at r: four parts in two pairs, the value (⊥, ⊤) and the relations (O, ⊑), with the lattice L it is given and the resolution r it is read at belonging to the reading and the sign to the act; an origin is (o, φ), and the poles are read, never stored: ⊥ is what is required joined with what its live claims hold, ⊤ what is signed met with what they allow; eight acts in four pairs and seven names answer for it: meet and join on the ceiling, local, a join only with a witness; observe and withdraw on the floor, local, a withdrawal being an observation at −1 that restores exactly; sign and require on both poles, travelling by rest, commuting and both closing freedom; encounter and refine with no pole; and no widening travels" at=policy:law/D11 by=target form=alphabet kind=definition measure=status needs=samples/yes/obligatory.json|samples/no/obligatory.json|vectors/moves.json restsOn=law/A0-carrier|law/A1-encounter|law/A2-meet|law/A4-epoch|law/A5-origin-is-extension|law/A7-freedom-conserved|law/A9-everything-is-a-bound role=demands scope=law/D11-the-obligatory value=present view=lattice
bound-lock/1 about="a signature narrows a ceiling and travels to every cell that rests on it as a meet, and meets do not remember the order they were taken in, so no order of any number of signatures ever shows in the field they leave; widening is not a meet and does not travel, which is why a narrowing costs one signature and an error costs one at every cell, and folding the field and signing it commute even with a withdrawal present" at=policy:law/T50 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T50-signatures-are-meets.json restsOn=law/A2-meet|law/A9-everything-is-a-bound|law/T19-signatures-fold role=demands scope=law/T50-signatures-are-meets value=present view=lattice
bound-lock/1 about="for a budget of origins there is a siting that minimises what a field cannot reach, and it is found by bridging the two largest islands in turn, because what an origin is worth is the product of the two sides it joins; in three hundred cells left with four thousand three hundred and eighty unreachable pairs, twelve origins dropped blindly closed between none and a fifth of them and the same twelve chosen by reach closed four fifths" at=policy:law/T51 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T51-the-shape-of-knowing-can-be-designed.json restsOn=law/T44-an-origin-is-worth-its-reach|law/T41-distance-is-the-walk-between-lookings|law/T45-cells-that-rest-on-one-bound-are-entangled|law/T49-amplitude-has-sign-and-phase role=demands scope=law/T51-the-shape-of-knowing-can-be-designed value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="a field left to itself concentrates where it already is and keeps its deserts: under attachment its horizon falls slowly and does not close, in sixty epochs and in either draw, while the same budget spent each epoch where reach is greatest closes it in four; the machine that does it holds nothing and asserts nothing, reads the field as it stands, answers only which two islands to bridge, and is itself a cell of the field it weaves" at=policy:law/T52 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T52-directing-where-origins-land-closes-the-horizon.json restsOn=law/T51-the-shape-of-knowing-can-be-designed|law/A6-vacuity|law/T44-an-origin-is-worth-its-reach|law/A9-everything-is-a-bound role=demands scope=law/T52-directing-where-origins-land-closes-the-horizon value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="the cells under the order of rest, with signatures as meets and the phase each origin carries as what they are enriched over, look like an enriched meet-semilattice, and what this library proves would be its representation theory; identity, composition, associativity, commuting and naturality hold for the operations as vectors, while observation is not one of them — it moves the metric and can split a cell no signature could, so it is a functor out of the category and not an arrow inside it, and the join, which does not travel, is a second kind of arrow this conjecture does not name" at=policy:law/H4 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/H4-enriched-semilattice.json|samples/no/H4-enriched-semilattice.json restsOn=law/T50-signatures-are-meets|law/T49-amplitude-has-sign-and-phase|law/T41-distance-is-the-walk-between-lookings role=demands scope=law/H4-enriched-semilattice value=present view=lattice
bound-lock/1 about="amplitudes with a phase and no origin, no signed ceiling, no resolution and no epoch band are what is left of a cell when those four fields are dropped, so the measurement problem is the absence of who, imposed symmetries the absence of a signed ceiling, the classical limit the absence of resolution and universal interference the absence of bands; restored, four claims in phase keep exactly the share of the whole their number leaves them against an environment spread over the period, and six origins around one value are six objects read finely and one read coarsely, so how many things there are is a reading; structural resemblance, one origin, not a claim about the world" at=policy:law/H5 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/H5-hilbert-is-the-obligatory-without-four-fields.json|samples/no/H5-hilbert-is-the-obligatory-without-four-fields.json restsOn=law/H3-a-distant-signature-moves-a-cell-that-did-not-move|law/T49-amplitude-has-sign-and-phase|law/T36-agreement-has-a-resolution|law/T45-cells-that-rest-on-one-bound-are-entangled role=demands scope=law/H5-hilbert-is-the-obligatory-without-four-fields value=present view=lattice
bound-lock/1 about="a lock is mostly settled: the form of most claims leaves them one legal state and they are applied, what the form leaves wider splits into those a reading has closed and those standing in force with nothing read against them, and the few that say of themselves that they are decisions are the only ones open; the four classes are a partition, every claim in exactly one, and a decision is not a claim with a wide ceiling but a claim that declares itself unanswered" at=policy:law/T53 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T53-a-decision-is-what-the-form-leaves-open.json restsOn=law/A0-carrier|law/A8-four-states|law/D3-state|law/T26-knowing-has-four-states role=demands scope=law/T53-a-decision-is-what-the-form-leaves-open value=present view=lattice
bound-lock/1 about="a tree is read by regions and not by leaves: what the lock names are regions, what the readers touch are the leaves those regions happen to hold, and on this tree there are several leaves to every region, so a tree that grows a thousand files does not grow a thousand questions and the cost of knowing it follows the regions and not the listing" at=policy:law/T58 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T58-observation-is-over-regions-by-reach.json restsOn=law/T41-distance-is-the-walk-between-lookings|law/A3-resolution|law/D1-region|law/T44-an-origin-is-worth-its-reach role=demands scope=law/T58-observation-is-over-regions-by-reach value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="a policy is four weights and nothing else, over the reach of a cell, how together its claims arrived, what stands beside it and what it still leaves free; the law is the relation, that a policy carrying all four closes at least as much as any policy carrying one and forks no more than those that close at all, and the counts belong to whoever reproduces it, here fifty-two closed against fifty-one and forty-eight with the fewest forks of the three" at=policy:law/T55 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T55-a-policy-is-four-weights.json restsOn=law/A1-encounter|law/T44-an-origin-is-worth-its-reach|law/T51-the-shape-of-knowing-can-be-designed|law/T49-amplitude-has-sign-and-phase role=demands scope=law/T55-a-policy-is-four-weights value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="how knowing moves through a field is one number, the forks it opens against the closes it makes, and that number tells regimes apart that no count of looks can: one policy over one field, with claims drawn near the meet, across it, or from two origins alone, separates into three regimes two orders apart" at=policy:law/T56 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T56-forks-over-closes-separates-regimes.json restsOn=law/T55-a-policy-is-four-weights|law/D7-fork|law/T27-disagreement-can-be-provoked|law/T36-agreement-has-a-resolution role=demands scope=law/T56-forks-over-closes-separates-regimes value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="the rule that makes the game is in the field and not above it: a cell one origin has claimed is grey and nothing that origin does alone will close it, so what an origin is worth is asymmetric, nothing over its own claims and everything over another-s, and the referee is a rule no player can suspend because it is the rule that makes a claim information" at=policy:law/T57 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T57-a-refereed-game-governs-itself.json restsOn=law/A1-encounter|law/A5-origin-is-extension|law/T55-a-policy-is-four-weights|law/T21-reading-is-an-origin role=demands scope=law/T57-a-refereed-game-governs-itself value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="who said it, when they said it and what is remembered are three coordinates of one claim and none of them is the claim: two origins saying one span are two claims and one origin saying it twice is one, so what a cell holds together depends on the spans alone while what it is depends on all three" at=policy:law/T63 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T63-author-time-memory-are-relative.json restsOn=law/A4-epoch|law/A5-origin-is-extension|law/D0-coordinate|law/T2-coordinate-where-disagree role=demands scope=law/T63-author-time-memory-are-relative value=present view=galois
bound-lock/1 about="to own a claim is to be the origin of it and nothing else: a cell holds what each origin said, taking an origin away takes exactly what it said and no more, and no narrowing survives the origin that made it" at=policy:law/T65 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T65-ownership-is-being-an-origin.json restsOn=law/A5-origin-is-extension|law/A1-encounter|law/D5-declaration|law/T8-exact-withdrawal role=demands scope=law/T65-ownership-is-being-an-origin value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="there is no after: what stands at a cell is what the latest epoch says and the order the claims arrived in never decides, so every order of one set of claims leaves one reading and a clock is not a fact about the field" at=policy:law/T66 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T66-there-is-no-after.json restsOn=law/A4-epoch|law/T22-fold-is-superposition|law/T50-signatures-are-meets|law/D8-present role=demands scope=law/T66-there-is-no-after value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="a withdrawal takes back what a claim did and never that it was made: the claim stays on the cell, the origin still spoke, and what changed is what the cell now means, which is why a withdrawal is a reinterpretation and not an erasure" at=policy:law/T67 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T67-withdrawal-is-reinterpretation.json restsOn=law/T8-exact-withdrawal|law/A4-epoch|law/A1-encounter|law/T19-signatures-fold role=demands scope=law/T67-withdrawal-is-reinterpretation value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="a gap is not the absence of a claim but a claim at the coarsest resolution: a cell nobody has narrowed holds the whole scale, which is exactly what saying nothing says, so a reading that is missing and a reading that allows everything are one line and a tree with gaps is a tree read coarsely" at=policy:law/T70 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T70-a-gap-is-a-coarse-claim.json restsOn=law/A6-vacuity|law/A3-resolution|law/D1-region|law/T5-coarsen-widens role=demands scope=law/T70-a-gap-is-a-coarse-claim value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="four instruments that share no mechanism fold the same way because a measurement is a cell: for a thermometer, a survey, an interferometer and a headcount the five fields are named without strain and the same five operations answer for all four; no number is claimed, only that the table can be filled in every row" at=policy:law/H6 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/H6-structure-of-measurement.json|samples/no/H6-structure-of-measurement.json restsOn=law/D11-the-obligatory|law/A0-carrier|law/A1-encounter|law/A3-resolution role=demands scope=law/H6-structure-of-measurement value=present view=lattice
bound-lock/1 about="what carries an encounter is a medium, and a medium is what two origins can both reach: in each instrument the medium can be named and the encounter happens where two origins touch it and nowhere else, so two origins at one cell make information and the same two at two cells make none; structural resemblance, one origin, not a claim about the world" at=policy:law/H7 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/H7-the-medium-of-encounters.json|samples/no/H7-the-medium-of-encounters.json restsOn=law/A1-encounter|law/T41-distance-is-the-walk-between-lookings|law/D1-region role=demands scope=law/H7-the-medium-of-encounters value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="a field of cells with origins and signatures is a game whose referee is inside it: a move is a claim, a claim alone is potential, two that meet are information, a signature moves every cell that rests on it, and no player may suspend the rule that makes the first four; the claim is that each of five readings of the field matches all five properties; structural resemblance, one origin, not a claim about the world" at=policy:law/H8 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/H8-refereed-game.json|samples/no/H8-refereed-game.json restsOn=law/T57-a-refereed-game-governs-itself|law/A1-encounter|law/T50-signatures-are-meets role=demands scope=law/H8-refereed-game value=present view=lattice
bound-lock/1 about="a cell that folds itself converges: observing each epoch a claim of width ten centred on its own meet and off by at most s, it narrows only when the offset cuts inside what it holds, so its freedom settles toward log2(11 − 2s) from above and it never conflicts; at s = 3, sixty epochs leave it between 2.38 and 2.43 bits on three seeds" at=policy:law/T73 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T73-a-cell-that-folds-itself-converges.json restsOn=law/A9-everything-is-a-bound|law/A7-freedom-conserved|law/A1-encounter role=demands scope=law/T73-a-cell-that-folds-itself-converges value=present view=galois
bound-lock/1 about="the obligatory is maximal: take away any one of its seven parts and what is left is an object already known, and anything added to it is either already inside it or breaks the four states" at=policy:law/H9 by=target form=alphabet kind=conjecture measure=status needs=samples/yes/H9-the-obligatory-is-maximal.json|samples/no/H9-the-obligatory-is-maximal.json restsOn=law/A8-four-states|law/A9-everything-is-a-bound|law/D11-the-obligatory role=demands scope=law/H9-the-obligatory-is-maximal value=present view=lattice
bound-lock/1 at=policy:law/formulas by=target form=formula measure=text role=writes scope=law/A2-meet/formula value="meet(c) = ⊤ ∧ ⋀_{o∈O} span_o"
bound-lock/1 at=policy:law/formulas by=target form=formula measure=text role=writes scope=law/A1-encounter/formula value="info(c) ⟺ |ext(O)| ≥ 2 ∧ meet(c) ≠ ∅"
bound-lock/1 at=policy:law/formulas by=target form=formula measure=text role=writes scope=law/D4-debit-in-bits/formula value="F(c) = log₂ |{x ∈ L : ⊥ ≤ x ≤ ⊤}|"
bound-lock/1 at=policy:law/formulas by=target form=formula measure=text role=writes scope=law/T50-signatures-are-meets/formula value="sign: ⊤(c′) ← ⊤(c′) ∧ s   ∀ c′ ⊒ c"
bound-lock/1 at=policy:law/formulas by=target form=formula measure=text role=writes scope=law/D11-the-obligatory/floor value="⊥(c) = ⋁ required ∨ ⋁_{o∈O} lo_o"
bound-lock/1 at=policy:law/formulas by=target form=formula measure=text role=writes scope=law/D11-the-obligatory/ceiling value="⊤(c) = ⋀ signed ∧ ⋀_{o∈O} hi_o"
bound-lock/1 at=policy:law/formulas by=target form=formula measure=text role=writes scope=law/A8-four-states/formula value="state(c) ∈ {FREE, REQUIRED, FORBIDDEN, CONFLICT}"
bound-lock/1 at=policy:law/formulas by=target form=formula measure=text role=writes scope=law/A0-carrier/formula value="x ⊨ c ⟺ ⊥ ⊑ x ⊑ ⊤"
bound-lock/1 at=policy:law/formulas by=target form=formula measure=text role=writes scope=law/A4-epoch/formula value="claim = (o, span, e), e ≺ e′ ⟺ e → e′"
bound-lock/1 at=policy:law/formulas by=target form=formula measure=text role=writes scope=law/A5-origin-is-extension/formula value="ext(o) = {(x, span_o(x))}, ext(o) = ext(o′) ⟹ o = o′"
bound-lock/1 at=policy:law/formulas by=target form=formula measure=text role=writes scope=law/A9-everything-is-a-bound/formula value="o ⊢_{r,e} c for o, c ∈ C, and ⊢ ∈ C"
bound-lock/1 at=policy:law/formulas by=target form=formula measure=text role=writes scope=law/A7-freedom-conserved/formula value="F(C) = Σ_{c∈C} F(c),   F(a(c)) ≤ F(c) for every act a that narrows"
bound-lock/1 at=policy:law/formulas by=target form=formula measure=text role=writes scope=law/T49-amplitude-has-sign-and-phase/formula value="A(c) = |Σ_{o∈O} s_o w_o e^{iφ_o}|²"
bound-lock/1 at=policy:law/formulas by=target form=formula measure=text role=writes scope=law/T95-signatures-live-where-they-are-signed/formula value="⊤(c) = ⋀_{b ⊑ c} signed(b) ∧ ⋀_{o∈O} hi_o,   one line per act"
bound-lock/1 at=policy:law/formulas by=target form=formula measure=text role=writes scope=law/T87-the-quarter-turn/formula value="|e^{ia} + e^{ib}|² < 2 ⟺ |a − b| > π/2"
bound-lock/1 at=policy:law/formulas by=target form=formula measure=text role=writes scope=law/D3-state/formula value="state(c) ∈ {FREE, REQUIRED, FORBIDDEN, CONFLICT}"
bound-lock/1 about="a withdrawal is the claim it takes back with its sign turned: landed in phase with it, the two leave nothing, the cell goes back to grey and every bit the claim closed is open again" at=policy:law/T85 by=target form=alphabet kind=corollary measure=status needs=samples/yes/T85-withdrawal-is-an-anti-claim.json|samples/no/T85-withdrawal-is-an-anti-claim.json restsOn=law/T49-amplitude-has-sign-and-phase role=demands scope=law/T85-withdrawal-is-an-anti-claim value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="two claims reinforce within a quarter turn of each other and cancel beyond it, since |e^{ia} + e^{ib}|² < 2 exactly when |a − b| > π/2: a fork is destructive interference, and a field is laminar while fewer than half its pairs lie beyond a quarter turn, forks over closes below one" at=policy:law/T87 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T87-the-quarter-turn.json|samples/no/T87-the-quarter-turn.json restsOn=law/T48-epoch-is-phase|law/T49-amplitude-has-sign-and-phase|law/A8-four-states role=demands scope=law/T87-the-quarter-turn value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="phases spread evenly give forks over closes of exactly one; above one is several coherences facing each other, and only a third coherence lowers it" at=policy:law/T88 by=target form=alphabet kind=corollary measure=status needs=samples/yes/T88-turbulence-is-factions.json|samples/no/T88-turbulence-is-factions.json restsOn=law/T87-the-quarter-turn role=demands scope=law/T88-turbulence-is-factions value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="disagreement is where to look: a policy that weights the cells whose origins lie beyond a quarter turn of each other closes more than one blind to them" at=policy:law/T89 by=target form=alphabet kind=corollary measure=status needs=samples/yes/T89-disagreement-is-where-to-look.json|samples/no/T89-disagreement-is-where-to-look.json restsOn=law/T87-the-quarter-turn role=demands scope=law/T89-disagreement-is-where-to-look value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="freedom is log₂ of the states between the poles, which is the cell's entropy: encounters lower it, vacuity raises it, and nothing else moves it; two paths interfere from phase alone, and that is lost once which path was taken is observed" at=policy:law/T90 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T90-freedom-is-entropy.json|samples/no/T90-freedom-is-entropy.json restsOn=law/D4-debit-in-bits|law/A7-freedom-conserved|law/T48-epoch-is-phase role=demands scope=law/T90-freedom-is-entropy value=present view=chain
bound-lock/1 about="many objects make a field: cells read pairwise meet or fork, the meets join them into components, and the whole can have no meet although most of its pairs do" at=policy:law/T91 by=target form=alphabet kind=corollary measure=status needs=samples/yes/T91-many-objects-make-a-field.json|samples/no/T91-many-objects-make-a-field.json restsOn=law/T92-a-cell-is-made-of-cells role=demands scope=law/T91-many-objects-make-a-field value=present view=product
bound-lock/1 about="origins, bounds, claims and rests are cells, and the state a cell shows is the meet of its parts' states; reading deeper is reading at a finer resolution, and it converges" at=policy:law/T92 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T92-a-cell-is-made-of-cells.json|samples/no/T92-a-cell-is-made-of-cells.json restsOn=law/A9-everything-is-a-bound|law/A3-resolution|law/A2-meet role=demands scope=law/T92-a-cell-is-made-of-cells value=present view=product
bound-lock/1 about="an act is a meet on its origin's own ceiling: the medium and the policy are cells too, reach is the meet of regions, being in phase the meet of bands and choosing what fits, and there is no third object" at=policy:law/T93 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T93-every-act-is-paid-by-its-origin.json|samples/no/T93-every-act-is-paid-by-its-origin.json restsOn=law/A2-meet|law/A5-origin-is-extension|law/T44-an-origin-is-worth-its-reach role=demands scope=law/T93-every-act-is-paid-by-its-origin value=present view=field
bound-lock/1 about="propagation of a sign or require halts at any cell where the new bound is absorbed (meet(a,b) = a), because every cell resting on it already carries a bound at least as tight; a region's bounds summarise as an interval (min ceiling, max floor) and a signature outside the interval never enters the region. Signing costs what it bites, never what lies beneath." at=policy:law/T94 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T94-a-signature-stops-where-the-meet-is-identity.json|samples/no/T94-a-signature-stops-where-the-meet-is-identity.json restsOn=law/A2-meet|law/T45-cells-that-rest-on-one-bound-are-entangled|law/T50-signatures-are-meets role=demands scope=law/T94-a-signature-stops-where-the-meet-is-identity value=present view=lattice
bound-lock/1 about="a signature or requirement is a line at the bound, never a value copied into resting cells; a cell's poles are read up its chain of rest as the meet of the live signatures above it; an absorbed signature stays live so withdrawing a tighter one reveals it. Signing and withdrawing cost one line; reading costs the depth of rest; nothing propagates, and A2 with T3 makes the reading equal to any replay." at=policy:law/T95 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T95-signatures-live-where-they-are-signed.json|samples/no/T95-signatures-live-where-they-are-signed.json restsOn=law/A2-meet|law/T3-fixed-point|law/T45-cells-that-rest-on-one-bound-are-entangled|law/T94-a-signature-stops-where-the-meet-is-identity role=demands scope=law/T95-signatures-live-where-they-are-signed value=present view=lattice
bound-lock/1 about="the fold is a monotone map on a lattice over a rest order with no cycles: every fold reaches its fixed point in finitely many steps and never fails to answer. The lock is not Turing complete by construction — it cannot loop — so verify can check it, rank can read it before landing, and accept can refuse before running. Arbitrary computation lives only in capsules, outside the fold, admitted by vectors and heard as claims." at=policy:law/T99 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T99-the-fold-is-total.json|samples/no/T99-the-fold-is-total.json restsOn=law/A2-meet|law/T9-self-application-converges|law/A9-everything-is-a-bound role=demands scope=law/T99-the-fold-is-total value=present view=lattice
bound-lock/1 about="an origin has finite looks per epoch; what it looks at closes a bit of the cell and a bit of itself, and what it stops looking at reopens by vacuity. Freedom plus what is closed is conserved exactly; the field settles where closing equals forgetting, so what one attention can hold real is bounded by its looks over the forgetting rate. The price of an act is attention, and the entropy goes to the grey." at=policy:law/T100 by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/yes/T100-an-act-is-paid-with-attention.json|samples/no/T100-an-act-is-paid-with-attention.json restsOn=law/T93-every-act-is-paid-by-its-origin|law/A6-vacuity|law/A7-freedom-conserved|law/T90-freedom-is-entropy role=demands scope=law/T100-an-act-is-paid-with-attention value=present view=chain
